        "original_id": "1eb4e3e9-8369-5453-95bd-d8d68ad25b50",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Jackson, Stephen G. Haw, Marco Polo\n- Organizations: Keele University, University of Keele\n- Roles: historian, scholar, Emeritus Professor of Medieval History, editor\n- Places: Newcastle-under-Lyme, Staffordshire, England, China, East Asia\n- Products: The Cambridge History of Iran: The Timurid and Safavid Periods\n- Topics: Crusades, Europeans and Mongols, medieval Muslim India, Mongol conquests, Marco Polo studies\n\nFacts:\n- Keele University was founded in 1949 as the University College of North Staffordshire.\n- Keele University was granted university status by Royal Charter in 1962.\n- Keele University, officially the University of Keele, is a public research university located about 3 miles from Newcastle-under-Lyme, Staffordshire, England.\n- Peter Jackson is a scholar and historian who specializes in the Crusades, contacts between Europeans and Mongols, and medieval Muslim India.\n- Peter Jackson is Emeritus Professor of Medieval History at Keele University.\n- Peter Jackson is the editor of The Cambridge History of Iran: The Timurid and Safavid Periods.\n- Stephen G. Haw made a major contribution to studies of Marco Polo's account of East Asia.\n- Peter Jackson, identified as an authority on the history of the Mongol conquests, said that Stephen G. Haw's book on Marco Polo must have settled the controversy over whether Marco Polo visited China.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
